# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# run artefacts and caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `_runs/` is where run_tests.py writes every failing suite's FULL output,
# named for the run, plus any diagnostic script a builder wrote. It is
# regenerated on every run and must never be committed.
_runs/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# The mutation engine's restore payloads and any half-written temp file. A run
# killed between mutate and restore leaves one of these behind; committing it
# would commit a deliberately broken source file.
mutbak
mutbak*
*.mutbak
*.tmp
*.tmp-*

# build output
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
*.whl
*.tar.gz

# environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
.python-version

# editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MEDIA AND SUBTITLE CONTENT - NEVER, UNDER ANY PATH
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two separate rules live here and only one of them is about disk space.
#
# 1. No real media in this workspace. The suites generate zero-byte stubs and
#    build real videos in a temp dir (spec/07-test-plan.md).
#
# 2. No subtitle CONTENT, ever. jimaku's files carry no stated licence and are
#    not ours to redistribute (LEDGER-HOT.md, THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md). hato
#    downloads them to the user's own machine and mirrors nothing - and the
#    quickest way to break that would be one stray `git add -A` from a folder
#    holding a run's output. Extension rules, not path rules: a path rule only
#    protects the directory somebody thought of.
#
# Nothing legitimate is blocked: every subtitle the suites touch is built in a
# temp dir, and the committed API fixtures are .json metadata.
*.mkv
*.mp4
*.m4v
*.avi
*.ts
*.m2ts
*.webm
*.mov
*.mka
*.opus
*.flac
*.aac
*.wav
*.mp3
*.srt
*.ass
*.ssa
*.vtt
*.sub
*.idx
*.sup
*.7z
*.zip
*.rar
*.tar
*.tgz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS - and this file is NOT what protects them
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The jimaku key lives at InfiniteVoid/keystore/hato-jimaku.txt, OUTSIDE every
# repository BY CONSTRUCTION - not by a rule in a file anyone can edit, and
# not by remembering. hato reads it at runtime from there or from
# $HATO_JIMAKU_KEY, and prints at most its last four characters.
#
# These lines are a second net, and they would not have saved the reference
# project's key: a `.gitignore` cannot un-commit anything, this workspace
# auto-commits every few minutes, and git history has no undo.
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
credentials.json
key.txt
hato-jimaku*.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# what is DELIBERATELY tracked, and must not be swept by a broader rule later
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# hato.config.json  - the SOURCE TREE's config. Committed, carries no secret,
#                     and never ships in the wheel (pyproject.toml explains).
# hato-run.cmd      - the Windows launcher. CRLF, see .gitattributes.
# tests/fixtures/   - recorded API response metadata, byte-exact.
